      "math_academy_id": "e-8553",
      "problem": "Given $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ compute $P(X = 3).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/e0b6722518c3fc07dcdb23e3d58aa963817b08ba0163c10439f74c691fb7bab2.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Geom}\\left(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14165669/assets/f51b669d0043918cb01345ea7f6a5881a6b419f4a604dab950681a8c47ad7655.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
